us\nShow submenu for Visit us\nOpen days and visits\nAttractions\nFor schools and colleges\nLocation\nAlumni\nLibrary and Collections\nBusiness School\nThings To Do\nAbout us\nHow to contact us\nSearch durham.ac.uk\nSearch\nClose search\nHome\nStudy\nDoctoral School\nStudy with us\nHow to apply\nDoctoral School\nExplore Doctoral School\nDoctoral School\nStudy with us\nHow to apply\nResearch opportunities\nTestimonials\nPostgraduate Events\nSubmit your application\nFunding and Scholarships\nStudentships\nDoctoral Training Programmes\nDoctoral journey\nWellbeing Support and Community\nGlobal opportunities\nCollege and community\nResearcher development and careers\nDurham Centre for Academic Development\nCareers enterprise and employability\nDeveloping engagement and impact skills\nCurrent researchers\nNews events and impact\nLatest news\nOur people\nContact us\nOpen menu\nStudy with us\nHow to apply\nResearch opportunities\nTestimonials\nPostgraduate Events\nSubmit your application\nFunding and Scholarships\nStudentships\nDoctoral Training Programmes\nDoctoral journey\nWellbeing Support and Community\nGlobal opportunities\nCollege and community\nResearcher development and careers\nDurham Centre for Academic Development\nCareers enterprise and employability\nDeveloping engagement and impact skills\nCurrent researchers\nNews events and impact\nLatest news\nOur people\nContact us\nStart your research journey at Durham\nJoining Durham as a postgraduate researcher offers the opportunity to work alongside leading academics in a world-class research environment. Explore the steps involved in applying, from developing your research proposal and identifying a supervisor.\nStep 1: Identify your research area\nExplore departments, centres and institutes to identify where your research interests are best aligned.\nExplore Academic Departments\nStep 2: Find a supervisor\nContact a potential supervisor whose expertise matches your proposed research project. Departments are happy to discuss research opportunities and supervisory support before application.\nFind a supervisor\nStep 3: Develop your research proposal (if required)\nPrepare a clear and compelling research proposal outlining:\nResearch aims and objectives\nBackground and rationale\nProposed methodology\nAnticipated contribution to knowledge\nPlease check with your potential supervisor and Department if this is required.\nStep 4: Check entry requirements\nMost applicants are expected to hold at least a UK 2:1 honours degree or international equivalent. Additional entry requirements may vary by programme. Please check with individual academic departments for entry requirements.\nInternational entry requirements\nEnglish language requirements\nStep 5: Submit your application\nApplications are submitted online through Durham University's Applicant Portal. Your application can be saved and completed in stages.\nDocuments you may need\nAcademic transcripts\nDegree certificates\nResearch proposal\nPersonal statement\nTwo references\nEnglish language evidence (where applicable)\nScholarship documents (if applicable)\nSubmit your application\nFunding opportunities and international guidance\nWe offer a range of funding opportunities, as well as guidance for international applicants on entry requirements and visa and immigration support.\nFunding and scholarships\nWe offer a range of funding opportunities including:\nDurham University Scholarships\nStudentships\nDoctoral Training Partnerships (DTPs)\nCentres for Doctoral Training (CDTs)\nInternational Funding Schemes\nWe encourage applicants to explore funding opportunities early as many schemes have application deadlines before programme start dates.\nExplore funding and scholarships\nInternational applicants\nDurham welcomes doctoral researchers from around the world and provides dedicated support for international applicants, including:\nCountry-specific entry requirements\nEnglish language guidance\nVisa and immigration support\nPre-arrival and orientation services\nOngoing student support throughout your studies\nInformation for international applicants\nTake the next step\nWhether you are refining a research idea, searching for funding, or preparing your application, Durham University provides an exceptional environment in which to pursue advanced research and become part of a thriving research community.\nApply now\nQuicklinks\nFind a supervisor\nResearch opportunities\nResearch degree programmes\nFunding and scholarships\nInternational applicants\nMeet our alumni\nContact Durham University\nAbout us\nDurham University on Bluesky\nDurham University on Twitter\nDurham University on Facebook\nDurham University on LinkedIn\nDurham University on YouTube\nDurham University on Instagram\nDurham University on TikTok\nThe University\nAbout us\nJobs\nContact us\nVisit us\nOur Colleges\nAcademic Departments\nCeremonies\nStatements and policies\nNotices\nStatement on Modern Slavery\nFreedom of expression\nWebsite accessibility\nStudent complaints and non-academic misconduct\nSafeguarding\nBusiness services\nHelping business\nAnalytical services\nGlobal Durham\nInternational Consortia\nResearch and partnerships\nUseful links\nLearn Ultra\nBanner Self-Service\nStaff directory\nTechnician Commitment\nDU Hub (Internal)\nIT help and support\nThe Palatine Centre\nDurham University\nStockton Road\nDurham\nDH1 3LE\nCharitable status\nDisclaimer\nTrading name\nCookie notice\nPrivacy notices\n\u00a92026 Durham University", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/study/doctoral-school/study-with-us/how-to-apply/#main-content"], ["", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/"], ["", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/"], ["Alumni", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/alumni/"], ["Library and Collections", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/departments/library/"], ["Business School", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/business/"], ["Things To Do", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/things-to-do/"], ["About us", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/about-us/"], ["How to